
A. E0 -- the entry's stated value against what RMG derives from the same entry
==============================================================================

  A1. the two paths
  -----------------
    entry.data.E0 as stored           : None (not stated)
    data.to_wilhoit(B=1000).E0        : 1108.0527 kJ/mol
    data.H298 as stored               : 1114.2470 kJ/mol
    5/2 R T at 298.15 K               : 6.1974 kJ/mol
    H298(stored) - derived E0         : +6.1943 kJ/mol

  A2. which one the runtime consumes
  ----------------------------------
    thermoengine.process_thermo_data sets spc.conformer.E0 = wilhoit.E0
    (rmgpy/thermo/thermoengine.py:75-78), and ThermoData.to_wilhoit
    (thermodata.pyx:366-389) reads Tdata/Cpdata/H298/S298 ONLY -- self.E0 is
    never consulted. So a stated E0 is inert on the path that matters and
    visible on the path that does not.

  A3. the same question asked of the sibling cation entry, for context
  --------------------------------------------------------------------
    [Arp] stated E0                   : 1520.5730 kJ/mol
    [Arp] derived E0                  : 1514.3867 kJ/mol
    [Arp] stated - derived            : +6.1863 kJ/mol
    -> the same collision, in a library this ticket must not edit.

